|-
| [[Sancho I of Sarta|Sancho I]] || 1180 || 1261 || 1228–1261 || [[House of Fuertelon]] || Consolidated the southern conquests and began the war with the [[Kingdom of Tamarin]].
|-
| [[Fernando I of Sarta|Fernando I]] || 1223 || 1294 || 1261–1294 || [[House of Fuertelon]] || Strengthened the mountain frontier, completed the annexation of Tamarin, and settled the frontier treaty with [[Kingdom of Jacan|Jacan]].
|-
| [[Alfonso I of Sarta|Alfonso I]] || 1258 || 1313 || 1294–1313 || [[House of Fuertelon]] || Ruled through the buildup to the [[Great Catholic Schism]] and the hardening of north-south church alignments.
|-
| [[Carlos I of Sarta|Carlos I]] || 1669 || 1716 || 1705–1716 || [[House of Fuertelon]] || Forced to abdicate after the [[Treaty of Bahia Alta]] and the [[War of the Isthmus]].
|-
| [[Maria I of Sarta|Maria I]] || 1684 || 1747 || 1716–1747 || [[House of Fuertelon]] || Ruled under the royal parliamentary court and consolidated the postwar settlement in Sarta.
|-
